<title>JAPAN: Denso driven higher by Toyota Motor's popularity.</title>
<headline>Denso driven higher by Toyota Motor's popularity.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Denso Corp, a member of the Toyota Motor Corp group, hit a year's high in Monday afternoon trade due to the popularity of Toyota, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0439 GMT, the shares were 60 yen higher at 2,630 yen, surpassing the previous high of 2,570.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors believe that if Toyota's business is booming, then its group firms will also do well and that expectation is making them seek the shares,&quot; a &quot;Big Four&quot; broker said.</p>
<p>Denso Corp is a leading producer of electric and electronic parts.</p>
